function souvenirsPage(){return `${heading('MUGS & LOCAL KEEPSAKES','A little of each state,<br>to take home.','Two Starbucks state mugs are the priorities. Add one or two small local finds along the route, with the retail tax already in the budget.')}
<div class="notice green"><h3>Your souvenir envelope: $65–90 total.</h3><p><strong>$45–60</strong> for both mugs including estimated retail tax, plus <strong>$20–30</strong> for local keepsakes. This is a separate category. Clothing and larger purchases are not included; add those before shopping.</p><a href="#budget">Open the separate food, souvenir and transportation budget</a></div>
<div class="two-col"><section class="info-panel"><span class="kicker">RHODE ISLAND · THURSDAY DEC 10</span><h2>Providence Place Starbucks</h2><p><strong>1 Providence Place, Providence</strong><br>Suggested stop: <strong>11:30am–noon</strong>, after your State House tour request and brief Waterplace photos, before the hotel rest.</p><p>Ask for the <strong>Rhode Island 14oz destination mug</strong>. Specify Discovery Series, or Been There if you are matching an existing collection. The mall lists Thursday hours 11am–8pm; check the individual Starbucks schedule in the official app / locator. The location is corroborated by a store listing, but the JavaScript-only locator did not expose live details to the research tool.</p><p><strong>Mug estimate:</strong> $20–25 + 7% tax = <strong>$21.40–26.75</strong>. Merchandise does not need a tip. Any drink is a separate meal-tax purchase.</p><p>Do not rely on an old listing for a Starbucks at your hotel: Hilton’s current dining page describes Shop+ instead. If this mall shop is out, ask staff which nearby store has the Rhode Island design before making another trip.</p>${link(map('Starbucks 1 Providence Place Providence RI'),'Directions to the Rhode Island mug stop','route-link')}${cite('starbucksRI','starbucksRIlisting','mall','starbucksMugs')}</section>
<section class="info-panel"><span class="kicker">CONNECTICUT · SATURDAY DEC 12</span><h2>Hartford Marriott Starbucks</h2><p><strong>200 Columbus Boulevard, Hartford · lobby</strong><br>Suggested stop: <strong>11:50am–12:10pm</strong>, after the Wadsworth and before lunch. About 5–10 minutes’ walk from the museum.</p><p>Marriott’s official page lists a Starbucks with a retail shop and Saturday hours <strong>6am–3pm</strong>. Ask for the <strong>Connecticut 14oz destination mug</strong>. The café is verified; Connecticut mug inventory is not.</p><p><strong>Mug estimate:</strong> $20–25 + 6.35% tax = <strong>$21.27–26.59</strong>. No merchandise tip.</p><p><strong>Backup:</strong> City Place Starbucks, <strong>185 Asylum Street</strong>, toward your lunch / Union Station area. Call ${link('tel:+18605271225','860-527-1225')} for mug stock and weekend opening: third-party schedules disagree, so do not leave it until late afternoon or Sunday.</p><p>No separate Hartford city design has been verified. The Connecticut state mug is the requested target; a store visit is not a stock guarantee.</p>${link(map('Starbucks Hartford Marriott Downtown 200 Columbus Boulevard Hartford CT'),'Directions to the Connecticut mug stop','route-link')}${cite('starbucksCT','starbucksCTbackup')}</section></div>
<div class="notice"><h3>What to ask before making a detour</h3><p>“Do you have the full-size Rhode Island / Connecticut destination mug in stock? Is it Discovery or Been There, what is the price before tax, and does it come boxed?” Ask whether staff can hold one if that store permits it. No stock check, phone call or hold has been made on your behalf.</p><p>Keep the box, ask for wrapping and carry the mugs cushioned in your day bag. Buy before the last morning rather than relying on airport stock.</p></div>
<div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT EACH PLACE IS KNOWN FOR</p><h2>Choose a souvenir with a story.</h2></div></div>
<div class="two-col"><section class="info-panel"><span class="kicker">RHODE ISLAND · OCEAN STATE</span><h3 class="serif">Coffee milk, craft & design.</h3><p><strong>Food identity:</strong> coffee milk, the official state drink, plus hot wieners, johnnycakes, pepper biscuits and coastal seafood traditions. Coffee syrup is distinctive, but a full bottle is less convenient for this flight itinerary; enjoy coffee milk there, or consider shipping a bottle.</p><p><strong>Providence identity:</strong> a major historic jewelry-manufacturing center and a city strongly associated with RISD and visual design. A small illustration or handmade piece makes more sense for your route than a distant shopping detour.</p><p><strong>My picks:</strong> your Rhode Island mug first; then a <strong>vintage Rhode Island postcard ($1.50 listed)</strong> or a small locally designed print. The RISD Store is at 30 North Main Street, near your afternoon museum area; its posted semester Thursday hours run until 7pm, but confirm the December schedule. Ask who made it and where rather than assuming every state-branded product was made locally.</p>${cite('riKnown','riJewelry','riPostcard','risdStore')}</section>
<section class="info-panel"><span class="kicker">CONNECTICUT · HARTFORD / RIVER VALLEY</span><h3 class="serif">Literary history, art & makers.</h3><p><strong>Hartford identity:</strong> Mark Twain’s literary legacy, historic architecture and the Wadsworth’s art collections. Statewide, Connecticut also has a strong artisan-gift and antiques tradition. Food signatures include New Haven-style pizza and hot-buttered lobster rolls; those are best enjoyed fresh rather than packed as souvenirs.</p><p><strong>My picks:</strong> your Connecticut mug first; then a <strong>Greetings from Hartford or Connecticut magnet ($6.95 listed)</strong> from the Wadsworth shop during your existing museum stop. A $10–20 maker ornament at Winterfair is a seasonal alternative.</p><p>A museum postcard, magnet or ornament is inexpensive, compact and easy to photograph for your trip diary. A Mark Twain-themed keepsake is a good alternative if you see one locally; no additional paid museum visit or gift-shop detour is required.</p>${cite('ctTwain','ctKnown','ctFood','ctMagnet','winterfair')}</section></div>
<div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">RETAIL PURCHASES · NO TIP ADDED</p><h2>The souvenir price list.</h2></div></div>
<p>Rhode Island standard merchandise tax: <strong>7%</strong>. Connecticut standard merchandise tax: <strong>6.35%</strong>. These are lower than the prepared-meal rates used on the food page. The estimates below assume ordinary taxable merchandise; qualifying art or food products can have different treatment. The actual receipt controls.</p>${cite('riSalesTax','ctTax')}
<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption class="sr-only">Souvenir prices before and after estimated retail sales tax</caption><thead><tr><th>Souvenir / where</th><th>Before tax</th><th>Retail tax</th><th>Estimated total</th></tr></thead><tbody>${SOUVENIRS.map(x=>{const r=x.state==='RI'?.07:.0635;const range=(a,b)=>a===b?money(a):money(a)+'–'+money(b);return `<tr><td><strong>${x.item}</strong><br>${x.where}<br><span class="muted">${x.status}</span></td><td>${range(x.low,x.high)}</td><td>${(r*100).toFixed(x.state==='RI'?0:2)}%<br>${range(x.low*r,x.high*r)}</td><td>${range(x.low*(1+r),x.high*(1+r))}</td></tr>`}).join('')}</tbody></table></div>
<div class="notice green"><h3>The two-mug math</h3><p>At the $20–25-per-mug allowance, Rhode Island tax adds $1.40–1.75 and Connecticut tax adds $1.27–1.59. The combined estimated checkout total is <strong>$42.67–53.34</strong>; the <strong>$45–60 reserve</strong> adds a little room. Exact Starbucks retail prices and your preferred series are not confirmed.</p><p>If a mug costs more than the allowance, compare the displayed price before buying. The table’s official online postcard / magnet prices are reference points, not confirmed local shelf inventory.</p></div>`}

const budgetRange = r => r[0] === r[1] ? money(r[0]) : `${money(r[0])}–${money(r[1])}`;
const dayFood = d => [0,1].map(i=>d.meals.reduce((sum,m)=>sum+m[i],0));
const foodEnvelope = [0,1].map(i=>BUDGET_DAYS.reduce((sum,d)=>sum+dayFood(d)[i],0));
const busEnvelope = [0,1].map(i=>BUDGET_DAYS.reduce((sum,d)=>sum+d.bus[i],0));
const planDefaults = {food:300,souvenirs:80,transit:25,taxis:95};
const planLabels = {food:'Food · all six days',souvenirs:'Souvenirs · both mugs + local gifts',transit:'Local buses · both cities',taxis:'Taxi reserve · airport + weather'};
let spendingPlan = {...planDefaults};
const storedPlan=readSaved('rict-spending-plan-v1',{});
for(const key of Object.keys(planDefaults)){const value=storedPlan?.[key];if(typeof value==='number'&&Number.isFinite(value)&&value>=0&&value<=5000)spendingPlan[key]=value;}
function planSummary(){const regular=spendingPlan.food+spendingPlan.souvenirs+spendingPlan.transit;return `<p class="plan-total">${money(regular+spendingPlan.taxis)} <span>your spending fund</span></p><p>${money(regular)} planned purchases + ${money(spendingPlan.taxis)} held for taxis. Reserve money is only spent if needed.</p>`;}
function budgetPage(){return `<div class="page-heading"><h1>Your spending budget.</h1><p>One traveler · December 9–14 · comfortable, casual meals and a few good finds. Lodging, flights and your booked Amtrak journey stay outside this budget.</p></div>
<div class="budget-lead"><h2>A $500 fund gives you room.</h2><p>Start with <strong>$300 food + $80 souvenirs + $25 local buses + $95 taxi reserve</strong>. That is a spending plan, not a predicted bill. Favor casual counters, enjoy one nicer dinner and use your included Hartford breakfasts.</p><p>Planning range: <strong>$335–465 for food, gifts and local buses</strong>. Hold <strong>$75–130 separately for taxis</strong>, for an overall fund of <strong>$410–595</strong>. Restaurant prices, shopping choices and weather decide where you land.</p></div>
<section class="budget-editor" aria-labelledby="budget-edit-title"><h2 id="budget-edit-title">Set your own amounts.</h2><p>Change any category to recalculate. Your choices save in this browser when storage is available. The meal and fare estimates below stay visible for comparison.</p><div class="budget-fields">${Object.entries(planLabels).map(([key,label])=>`<label for="budget-${key}">${label}<span class="currency-field"><span aria-hidden="true">$</span><input id="budget-${key}" data-budget="${key}" type="number" min="0" max="5000" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" value="${spendingPlan[key]}" aria-describedby="budget-help"></span></label>`).join('')}</div><p id="budget-help" class="muted">USD, per trip. Enter $0–5,000 per category. These are budget amounts, not an expense tracker.</p><div id="budget-result" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">${planSummary()}</div><button type="button" data-budget-reset>Reset to the $500 plan</button></section>
<section class="budget-section" aria-labelledby="food-budget-title"><h2 id="food-budget-title">Food: ${budgetRange(foodEnvelope)} for six days.</h2><p>Allowances below include estimated meal tax, 18% on seated meals and a little room for an optional counter tip. Coffee and treats are already counted. They are planning ranges, not verified menu quotes. Water instead of paid drinks helps; alcohol, delivery and unusual service fees need extra room.</p><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Daily meal budget, scroll horizontally on small screens"><table class="budget-table"><caption>Food by meal · USD · included hotel breakfast counts as $0 extra</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Day</th><th scope="col">Breakfast</th><th scope="col">Lunch</th><th scope="col">Dinner</th><th scope="col">Coffee / snacks</th><th scope="col">Food total</th></tr></thead><tbody>${BUDGET_DAYS.map(d=>`<tr><th scope="row">${d.date}</th>${d.meals.map(m=>`<td>${budgetRange(m)}</td>`).join('')}<td><strong>${budgetRange(dayFood(d))}</strong></td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody><tfoot><tr><th scope="row" colspan="5">Six-day food allowance</th><td><strong>${budgetRange(foodEnvelope)}</strong></td></tr></tfoot></table></div>
<details ${printing?'open':''}><summary>What each day’s food allowance buys</summary><div class="detail-body">${BUDGET_DAYS.map(d=>`<p><strong>${d.date}:</strong> ${d.note}</p>`).join('')}<p>Thursday’s planned lunch is East Side Pockets on Thayer Street; the Malted Barley’s published $15 turkey sandwich is the downtown bad-weather fallback. Saturday’s café lunch replaces Black-Eyed Sally’s to make room for Salute. A full Sally’s lunch or a second café order may exceed that day’s allowance.</p></div></details><p>The Providence hotel’s possible $10 daily credit is not deducted until eligibility is confirmed. Monday’s early departure does not assume the hot buffet is open.</p><p><a href="#food">Open the food shortlist and tax/tip calculator</a></p>${cite('riSalesTax','riTax','ctTax','hotelCT','hotelRI')}</section>
<section class="budget-section" aria-labelledby="souvenir-budget-title"><h2 id="souvenir-budget-title">Souvenirs: $65–90, kept separate.</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Two state mugs, plus one or two local keepsakes</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Purchase</th><th scope="col">Allowance</th><th scope="col">How to use it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Rhode Island + Connecticut Starbucks mugs</th><td>$45–60 total</td><td>Both mugs together, including estimated retail tax and a small price buffer.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Local cards, magnet or a small maker gift</th><td>$20–30 total</td><td>Split between states however you like. No requirement to buy in every shop.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Clothing / extra shopping</th><td>$0 in this plan</td><td>Browse freely. Add a separate amount if you want a sweatshirt, shoes or a larger purchase.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>No tip on ordinary merchandise. The mug price and stock remain unconfirmed; compare the shelf price before buying. Café purchases belong to food, not souvenirs.</p><p><a href="#souvenirs">See mug stops, retail tax and local gift ideas</a></p></section>
<section class="budget-section" aria-labelledby="transport-budget-title"><h2 id="transport-budget-title">Transportation: buses + a taxi reserve.</h2><p>The planned bus fares add up to <strong>${budgetRange(busEnvelope)}</strong>. Set aside <strong>$15–25</strong> for local fares and a little fare/loading flexibility. Wave funds you load but do not use are still tied up in the app. The separate taxi reserve below is essential to the airport plan.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Local transport by day · walking costs $0</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Day</th><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Bus allowance</th></tr></thead><tbody>${BUDGET_DAYS.map(d=>`<tr><th scope="row">${d.date}</th><td>${d.busNote}</td><td>${budgetRange(d.bus)}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div>
<h3>Hold $75–130 for taxis.</h3><ul><li><strong>$50–90:</strong> a direct East Hartford hotel → Bradley ride if needed. This is a planning allowance, not a fare quote.</li><li><strong>$25–40:</strong> one or more short city/weather transfers, depending on actual quotes. More rides or surge pricing can exceed this.</li></ul><p>If taking the 5am Bradley Flyer, a taxi to its downtown stop also comes from this reserve. Compare that full cost with a direct airport taxi. A direct taxi replaces the $1.75 airport bus purchase; it is not an extra required journey. Your bus envelope keeps that small amount as slack.</p><p>Keep the reserve until Monday’s airport pickup is secured. Do not count an unconfirmed hotel shuttle as a free ride. Flights and the booked Providence → New Haven → Hartford train are excluded, with no additional rail tickets planned.</p><p><a href="#transit">See trains versus buses, fares and the airport connection</a></p>${cite('wave','ct','flyer')}</section>
<div class="notice green"><h3>Keep sightseeing spending optional.</h3><p>RISD’s free Thursday window and the Wadsworth’s $0 order remain in the plan. Winterfair’s admission cost still needs checking. The optional December 11 Wolf Pack College Night has an advertised $20 all-in ticket offer. Set aside $520 instead of the base $500 if choosing it, subject to ticket availability. The separate .edu student offer is not assumed to apply to you. Pick either Bear’s dinner or the advertised $3 arena hot dogs rather than budgeting two full dinners. Cinema and other paid extras remain outside the base plan.</p></div>`;}
function updateBudget(){const el=document.getElementById('budget-result');if(!el)return;let valid=true;for(const key of Object.keys(planDefaults)){const input=document.getElementById('budget-'+key);const value=Number(input.value);const ok=input.value!==''&&Number.isFinite(value)&&value>=0&&value<=5000;input.setAttribute('aria-invalid',String(!ok));if(ok)spendingPlan[key]=value;else valid=false;}if(!valid){el.innerHTML='<p>Enter an amount from $0 to $5,000 in every category to calculate your fund.</p>';return;}save('rict-spending-plan-v1',spendingPlan);el.innerHTML=planSummary();}
function studentHangouts(){return `<section class="budget-section" aria-labelledby="verified-student-stops"><h2 id="verified-student-stops">Student & sports hangouts, checked.</h2><p>The main daytime choices are East Side Pockets → Ceremony in Providence, and Bloom, Story and Soil and Bear’s in Hartford. Antonio’s is a cheaper lunch alternative. For an organized college-oriented sports crowd, the best date match is Friday’s Wolf Pack College Night.</p>
<h3>Providence · Thursday, December 10</h3><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Providence student stops and published prices"><table><caption>Published menu prices checked November 18 · tax estimates shown separately from menu prices</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Place / evidence</th><th scope="col">Verified order and price</th><th scope="col">Where it fits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">East Side Pockets<br>278 Thayer Street</th><td>Falafel wrap $9.26. A plain sample online cart showed $0.74 tax + $1 processing = <strong>$11 total before tip</strong>. Chicken kabob / gyro wrap $12.04 before tax.</td><td>Planned lunch about 1:20–2pm. Brown University calls it a student favorite. ${cite('brownFood','pocketsMenu','pocketsHours')}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Antonio’s Pizza<br>256 Thayer Street</th><td>Cheese slice <strong>$3.99</strong>; two slices $7.98, about <strong>$8.62 with RI tax</strong>. Pepperoni slice $4.99.</td><td>Alternate lunch in the same Thayer loop. Brown’s student account supports the campus connection. Thursday uses normal prices, not the Wednesday promotion. ${cite('antoniosMenu','antoniosStudents')}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Ceremony · Brook Street<br>406 Brook Street</th><td>Americano <strong>$4.50</strong> / about $4.86 with RI tax. Latte $6.25 / about $6.75 with tax. Optional tips or online fees extra.</td><td>Your one café stop around 2–2:40pm, then descend toward RISD. Student interviews document the café as a working/social spot. Thu venue hours 8am–6:30pm. ${cite('ceremonyMenu','ceremonyHours','studentCafes')}</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h3>Hartford · Friday through Sunday</h3><div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Hartford student and sports stops with published prices"><table><caption>University-backed daytime stops, a public campus option, and one evening sports add-on</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Place / evidence</th><th scope="col">Verified cost</th><th scope="col">Where it fits</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Bear’s Smokehouse<br>25 Front Street</th><td>Posted classic sandwich <strong>$12</strong> + side <strong>$4</strong> = $16, about <strong>$17.18 with CT tax</strong>, optional tip extra.</td><td>Friday early dinner; Sunday dinner remains an easy repeat. Trinity’s student-written guide recommends it. ${cite('bearsMenu','ctStudentFood')}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wolf Pack College Night<br>PeoplesBank Arena</th><td>Official AXS advertises a <strong>$20 all-in offer</strong> for Dec 11, subject to seats. Friday promotion: <strong>$3 hot dogs</strong> through first intermission; check any concession tax at the stand.</td><td>Optional Friday evening: doors 6pm, game 7pm vs Rochester. AHL men’s hockey with a marketed college night. No student discount or .edu eligibility assumed, and no tickets purchased. ${cite('wolfGame','wolfOffer','wolfDeals')}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Bloom Bake Shop<br>80 Pratt Street</th><td>BLT <strong>$12</strong> + 12oz drip <strong>$3.50</strong> = about <strong>$16.64 with CT tax</strong>. 12oz latte $4.75 before tax.</td><td>Saturday lunch about 12:20–1:10pm, with Hartford Prints afterward. Trinity’s student guide recommends the street and café. Sat 8am–4pm. ${cite('bloomMenu','bloomCoffee','ctStudentPratt')}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Story and Soil<br>387 Capitol Avenue</th><td>Official-linked Hartford pickup menu: Americano <strong>$5.56</strong> / estimated $5.97 with CT tax; 12oz latte <strong>$6.36</strong> / estimated $6.83. Optional tips/checkout fees extra.</td><td>Sunday 10:30–11:10am before Parkville. Trinity’s student guide recommends it. Current venue hours Sun 8am–4pm. ${cite('storyMenu','storySoil','ctStudentFood')}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Trinity College · Raether Library / Peter B’s<br>300 Summit Street campus</th><td><strong>$0 for a library/campus visit.</strong> A café purchase is separate; no coffee price is invented here.</td><td>Optional Friday afternoon alternative to the river loop, only if the live bus leaves enough time. Trinity explicitly welcomes visitors to its campus cafés; library visitor access is weekdays 8am–6pm. Café operation is separate from library access. ${cite('ctCommunity')}</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<details ${printing?'open':''}><summary>Sports dates checked before choosing the Hartford event</summary><div class="detail-body"><p>Brown lists men’s basketball vs Wheaton at Pizzitola on Wednesday, December 9 at 6pm. That is tight after your 3:34pm airport arrival, so it is not in the main route. UConn men’s basketball vs Kansas on December 12 is in Storrs, not downtown Hartford. Friday’s downtown Wolf Pack College Night fits your actual Hartford stay.</p><p>Campus cafés are documented student spaces; the sports match is the direct athlete/sports setting. There is no source-backed basis to claim specific athletes regularly eat at any listed restaurant.</p>${cite('brownSports','uconnSports','wolfGame')}</div></details></section>`;}

function explorePage(){return `<div class="page-heading"><h1>Student hangouts,<br>cafés and sports.</h1><p>Your daytime shortlist: coffee, inexpensive food, browsing and places with a creative or college-adjacent feel. Prioritize one good neighborhood loop over a long checklist.</p></div>
<div class="notice green"><h2>Providence is the stronger match for your brief.</h2><p>My recommendation is to prioritize <strong>Thayer Street / College Hill</strong>, then Wickenden Street if there is time. Their university setting and mix of casual food and shops make them the best fit for the 18–25 atmosphere you described. Hartford’s documented student recommendations include <strong>Bear’s, Story and Soil and Bloom</strong>; Friday’s College Night adds the sports setting.</p><p>The shortlist below distinguishes university recommendations, student reporting and an advertised College Night. That evidence supports a student or sports atmosphere; it does not establish the age, gender or athlete status of every customer.</p>${cite('brownFood','studentCafes','ctStudentFood','wolfGame')}</div>
${studentHangouts()}
<section class="neighborhood-section" aria-labelledby="pvd-explore"><h2 id="pvd-explore">Providence · start on College Hill.</h2><article class="neighborhood-row"><div><h3>Thayer Street + Brown’s public streets</h3><p class="muted">Best fit for student-area cafés, casual food and browsing</p></div><div><p>The district sits beside Brown and RISD and mixes quick food, book browsing and shops. Start around Thayer and Angell, browse the Brown Bookstore, check the storefronts that interest you and choose one snack stop. <strong>Your chosen lunch is East Side Pockets, 278 Thayer Street.</strong> Order a falafel wrap and water, then browse nearby. Brown University’s own visitor guide calls it a student favorite. The university recommendation is stronger evidence than location alone.</p><p><strong>Spend:</strong> $0 to browse; the verified sample online falafel-wrap total was $11 including tax and a $1 online fee. Ceremony’s published Americano is $4.50 before tax ($4.86 with estimated RI meal tax). Clothing and bookstore merchandise come from extra shopping money.</p><p><strong>When:</strong> Thursday: leave the hotel at 12:45pm, allow 30–40 minutes to reach East Side Pockets, eat around 1:20–2pm, then browse Thayer until 2:50pm. Descend via Benefit Street from 3–4pm, with time to warm up before RISD at 5pm. The earlier sandwich lunch and pedestrian-bridge detour are replaced.</p><p>Brown’s calendar places classes through December 11 and final exams beginning December 12. Your Thursday visit is before winter recess, but end-of-term work can make the atmosphere quieter.</p>${link(map('Thayer Street and Angell Street Providence'),'Map Thayer Street','route-link')} · <a href="#itinerary/dec-10">Open Thursday’s route</a><p><a href="#food/east-pockets">See your order, tax and optional tip</a></p>${cite('brownFood','pocketsMenu','pocketsHours','ceremonyMenu','brownDates')}</div></article>
<article class="neighborhood-row"><div><h3>Wickenden Street / Fox Point</h3><p class="muted">Artier independent-shop alternative</p></div><div><p>Choose this as an alternative to the Thayer lunch-and-browsing loop if you would rather explore Fox Point’s independent shops and cafés. East Side Pockets remains the main itinerary choice. The state tourism guide describes its arts and independent-business character. This is a good alternative if shops and coffee matter more to you than the Brown campus setting.</p><p><strong>Spend:</strong> $0 to browse; one $5–10 café stop from your food allowance. Keep any purchase inside your gift envelope.</p><p><strong>When:</strong> Thursday early afternoon as a swap for the Thayer loop, with a different nearby lunch; not another hour added to the main route. Pick Thayer or a longer Wickenden browse if the cold or your energy limits walking.</p>${link(map('Wickenden Street Providence'),'Map Wickenden Street','route-link')}${cite('wickenden')}</div></article>
<article class="neighborhood-row"><div><h3>Downcity / Westminster + Providence Place</h3><p class="muted">Convenient browsing near your hotel</p></div><div><p>Use Westminster for a short shop-and-food stroll near your hotel, and Providence Place for indoor shopping and your Rhode Island mug hunt. For your interests, prioritize the local streets; the mall is the practical warm backup for familiar retail.</p><p><strong>Spend:</strong> window-shopping is free. Your Rhode Island mug is already in the $45–60 two-mug allowance. There is no clothing budget unless you add one.</p><p><strong>When:</strong> keep Thursday’s 11:30am mug stop; use short gaps near the hotel for Downcity rather than replacing the afternoon student district.</p>${link(map('Westminster Street Providence'),'Map Downcity shops','route-link')} · <a href="#souvenirs">Open mug details</a>${cite('mall')}</div></article></section>
<section class="neighborhood-section" aria-labelledby="ct-explore"><h2 id="ct-explore">Hartford · choose specific pockets.</h2><article class="neighborhood-row"><div><h3>Pratt Street · Bloom + Hartford Prints</h3><p class="muted">Best compact café-and-shop stop in this itinerary</p></div><div><p>Have a BLT and coffee at Bloom, 80 Pratt Street, then browse Hartford Prints at 42½ Pratt Street for local cards and gifts. Bloom’s counter and dining room make this a useful warm pause. Trinity’s own neighborhood guide recommends Bloom and Pratt Street to its students.</p><p><strong>Spend:</strong> $12 BLT + $3.50 12oz drip coffee = $15.50 menu subtotal, approximately $16.64 with CT meal tax before optional tip. The published 12oz latte is $4.75 instead of $3.50 for drip. Gifts come from the $20–30 local-keepsake envelope.</p><p><strong>When:</strong> Saturday lunch, after the Connecticut mug stop and before Winterfair. Bloom currently lists Tuesday–Saturday 8am–4pm and Sunday 8am–3pm; closed Monday. Check Hartford Prints’ current shop hours before going.</p>${link(map('Bloom Bake Shop 80 Pratt Street Hartford'),'Map Pratt Street cafés','route-link')} · <a href="#itinerary/dec-12">Open Saturday’s route</a>${cite('bloomMenu','bloomCoffee','hartfordPrints','ctStudentPratt')}</div></article>
<article class="neighborhood-row"><div><h3>Parkville Market</h3><p class="muted">Casual food choices and shared indoor seating</p></div><div><p>Make this your relaxed food-hall outing: compare the displayed menus, choose one meal and sit somewhere warm. The current vendor list includes noodle soup, mofongo, poke, tacos and boba options. The common seating makes it a better social-space bet than an isolated takeaway counter, though the ages will vary.</p><p><strong>Spend:</strong> Thai Street Food / Pho King Spot’s official-linked pickup menu lists Chicken Pho at $18.25, approximately $19.59 with CT meal tax before optional tip/checkout fees. Story and Soil is now the planned café stop beforehand; skip extra boba if keeping that same snack envelope.</p><p><strong>When:</strong> Sunday lunch, already in your route. Food vendors currently list Sunday 11am–8pm. Allow 30–60 minutes from downtown including bus waiting; use the local day pass and check Sunday service. Do not assume weekday $10 offers apply.</p>${link(map('Parkville Market 1400 Park Street Hartford'),'Map Parkville Market','route-link')} · <a href="#itinerary/dec-13">Open Sunday’s route</a>${cite('parkville')}</div></article>
<article class="neighborhood-row"><div><h3>Story and Soil · your Sunday café stop</h3><p class="muted">Independent coffee, small space</p></div><div><p>This independent café at 387 Capitol Avenue describes a 500-square-foot space: choose it for coffee and a local atmosphere, with a backup if the seats are full. Trinity’s student-written admissions guide recommends it; use the current venue hours rather than the older hours in that article.</p><p><strong>Spend:</strong> The official site’s linked Hartford pickup menu lists an Americano at $5.56 (about $5.97 with CT meal tax), or a 12oz latte at $6.36 (about $6.83 with tax). These estimates exclude optional tip and any checkout fee. Current Sunday venue hours are 8am–4pm.</p><p><strong>When:</strong> Sunday 10:30–11:10am, then use the live bus to Parkville for lunch around noon. Omit the café if weather or a long bus wait makes that connection impractical.</p>${link(map('Story and Soil Coffee 387 Capitol Avenue Hartford'),'Map Story and Soil','route-link')}${cite('storyMenu','storySoil','ctStudentFood')}</div></article></section>
<section class="budget-section"><h2>Cheap breakfast and lunch, with published prices.</h2><p>Ellie’s Signature Breakfast Sandwich is $7 before RI tax; Bloom’s egg-and-cheese sandwich is $9 before CT tax; Bear’s classic sandwich is $12 before CT tax. These are specific published orders. More expensive café drinks and add-ons are separate choices, so a college address does not automatically mean a cheaper bill.</p><p><a href="#food">Open all verified orders, meal tax and tip calculations</a></p>${cite('elliesMenu','bloomMenu','bearsMenu')}</section>
<section class="budget-section" aria-labelledby="student-base-title"><h2 id="student-base-title">Where are students based?</h2><p><strong>Providence:</strong> College Hill’s Brown/RISD setting makes Thayer the clearest public-facing starting point. Wickenden in Fox Point offers a different independent-shop loop nearby. Those commercial streets are more useful to visit than looking for particular student residences.</p><p><strong>Hartford:</strong> student activity is spread across UConn’s downtown campus, Trinity south of downtown and the University of Hartford’s campus near the Hartford / West Hartford / Bloomfield boundary. That geography is why I recommend specific cafés and food stops rather than promising one continuous student district.</p><p>For your hotel base, keep the existing stays. In East Hartford, plan the river crossing and return trip before setting out; the hotel itself is not the café/shopping district.</p>${cite('thayer','wickenden','uconnHartford','trinityCampus','uhart')}</section>
<div class="notice"><h2>Dining or shopping?</h2><p><strong>Providence:</strong> prioritize casual dining plus Thayer/Wickenden browsing. <strong>Hartford:</strong> prioritize the food hall, cafés, free art and a few local gifts. For this budget, both cities work better as food-and-neighborhood outings than as big clothing-shopping trips.</p><p>Browse first, buy selectively and keep the two state mugs as your souvenir priorities. <a href="#budget">Set your food, shopping and transportation amounts</a>.</p></div>`;}

function updateBill(){const el=document.getElementById('bill-result');if(!el)return;const value=document.getElementById('subtotal').value;const b=Number(value),rate=document.getElementById('state').value==='RI'?.08:.0735,t=Number(document.getElementById('tip').value);if(value===''||!Number.isFinite(b)||b<0||b>10000){el.innerHTML='<p>Enter a subtotal from $0 to $10,000.</p>';return}el.innerHTML=`<p class="calc-result">${money(b*(1+rate+t))} <span style="font:14px var(--sans)">estimated total</span></p><p class="muted" style="font-size:14px">Food ${money(b)} + tax ${money(b*rate)} + tip ${money(b*t)}</p>`}
function render(){const [route='overview',id]=location.hash.slice(1).split('/');let actual=['overview','itinerary','transit','food','weather','bookings','sources','souvenirs','budget','explore'].includes(route)?route:'overview';if(actual==='food'&&id)activeFood='All';main.innerHTML=({overview,transit,weather,bookings,budget:budgetPage,explore:explorePage,sources:sourcesPage,souvenirs:()=>souvenirsPage(),itinerary:()=>dayView(id),food:()=>foodPage(id)})[actual]();document.querySelectorAll('[data-nav]').forEach(a=>{const active=a.dataset.nav===actual;a.classList.toggle('active',active);if(active)a.setAttribute('aria-current','page');else a.removeAttribute('aria-current')});document.title=`${({overview:'A little New England winter',budget:'Spending budget',explore:'Student hangouts & shopping',itinerary:'Day by day',transit:'Getting around',food:'Good food',weather:'Winter & photos',bookings:'Booked travel',sources:'Sources & checks',souvenirs:'Mugs & souvenirs'})[actual]} · RI / CT`;updateBill();if(actual==='food'&&id){requestAnimationFrame(()=>document.getElementById('meal-'+id)?.scrollIntoView({block:'start'}))}}
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target.closest('.skip')){e.preventDefault();main.focus({preventScroll:true});main.scrollIntoView({block:'start',behavior:'instant'});return}const w=e.target.closest('[data-weather]');if(w){const y=window.scrollY;cold=w.dataset.weather==='cold';render();window.scrollTo(0,y);document.querySelector(`[data-weather="${cold?'cold':'normal'}"]`)?.focus({preventScroll:true})}const f=e.target.closest('[data-food]');if(f){const y=window.scrollY;activeFood=f.dataset.food;main.innerHTML=foodPage();updateBill();window.scrollTo(0,y);document.querySelector(`[data-food="${activeFood}"]`)?.focus({preventScroll:true})}});
document.addEventListener('change',e=>{if(e.target.matches('[data-check]')){checks[e.target.dataset.check]=e.target.checked;save('rict-checks',checks)}if(e.target.matches('#state,#tip'))updateBill()});document.addEventListener('input',e=>{if(e.target.id==='subtotal')updateBill();if(e.target.matches('[data-budget]'))updateBudget()});
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target.closest('[data-budget-reset]')){spendingPlan={...planDefaults};for(const key of Object.keys(planDefaults))document.getElementById('budget-'+key).value=spendingPlan[key];updateBudget();}});
window.addEventListener('hashchange',()=>{render();if(!location.hash.startsWith('#food/')){window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'instant'});main.focus({preventScroll:true})}});
document.getElementById('print').addEventListener('click',()=>{const previousFood=activeFood;activeFood='All';printing=true;main.innerHTML=overview()+DAYS.map(d=>`<div style="break-before:page">${dayView(d.id)}</div>`).join('')+budgetPage()+explorePage()+transit()+foodPage()+weather()+souvenirsPage()+bookings()+sourcesPage();window.print();printing=false;activeFood=previousFood;render()});
render();
if('serviceWorker'in navigator&&location.protocol!=='file:')navigator.serviceWorker.register('sw.js').catch(()=>{});
